  "term": "hazard analysis",
  "definition": "Hazard analysis is a statistical method used in mental health research to examine how different factors are related to the chance of an event happening over time, such as a suicide reattempt during follow-up. In this packet, it refers to Cox proportional hazard analysis for identifying risk factors linked with when reattempts occur.",
